  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Lagos Street Arcade",
    "overview": "Junction 101 is a Lagos street at night seen as an arcade: midnight navy ground, gold light pooling under lamps and on the one thing you should press, danfo yellow and Ankara cloth as the city's own colour. The look is user-pinned: the owner designed the welcome and sign-in in Google Stitch (\"Lagos Street Arcade\") and approved its palette, Outfit, the logo and the isometric building art. That pin supersedes the earlier Wax-Print Selvedge world for type, palette and imagery. Dark is the product's own look, not a theme setting; there is no light mode to fall back to.\n\nThe arcade is a game skin over a working shop and a real merchant directory, so it stays legible and operational. Sections sit flat on the navy ground divided by hairlines; only the city itself (the map frame, place headers, the welcome brand card) is raised. Three pieces carry over from the previous world and still define it: the market wax-print circle repeat as cloth (welcome panel, place headers), the selvedge truth strip that prints each surface's one plain rule, and exact-time bars. Players wear DiceBear Personas avatars.\n\nThe world refuses the fintech white-card default and the generic neon-cyber game skin. Gold glows softly; nothing is neon, nothing is chrome.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Midnight navy ground with two navy panel steps; gold is the one action and the coin colour.",
      "Outfit throughout, heavy and uppercase for calls to action and the brand lockup; tabular figures everywhere.",
      "Raster isometric Lagos art from Stitch on a 2:1 isometric road ground; name plates on every place.",
      "Pill-shaped controls; plates and frames with moderate rounding.",
      "A selvedge strip on every surface stating its one rule (gold on navy; solid gold band on the mobile welcome).",
      "Coins are game money: shown as a number with a coin icon and the words \"City Coins\", never with a currency symbol."
